# tally 2.3.1 S17, P22 B3 (L §5.11: mean keeps its terms' unit; §3.3 a rate's class with it): the mean of two
# yearly rates is a yearly rate, so a check prints 0.03 /year (a2) and periodic takes it (a3 0.03). Before: a2
# printed `0.03 1/year`, a3 RUN-DOMAIN `periodic: 0.03 1/year is not a rate`.
=== b3.tally
model w8
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "probe"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [k1, k2]
input r[k in ks]: rate
input pct: num %
input base: money PLN
def fee: num PLN = base * pct

ask a1: mean(r[k] for k in ks) + r[k1]
ask a2: check mean(r[k] for k in ks) == r[k2]
ask a3: periodic(mean(r[k] for k in ks), year, effective)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r[k1] = 2 %/year "s"
  r[k2] = 4 %/year "s"
  pct = 1 % "s"
  base = 300.00 PLN "s"
=== expect
a1: 0.05 /year
  cut 2026-06-30
a2: differs: mean(r[k] for ...) = 0.03 /year, r[k2] = 0.04 /year, difference -0.01 /year
  cut 2026-06-30
a3: 0.03
  cut 2026-06-30
